            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "When I share logic with the `VimEnter` handler, I get stopped somewhere. Still investigating.\r\n\r\nMy agent wants me to edit the C code...\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>LLM suggestion</summary>\r\n\r\nThe underlying bug is an empty short filename, not directory rendering.\r\n\r\n  The sequence is:\r\n\r\n  1. Directory full names now end with a separator in `src/nvim/buffer.c:3621`.\r\n  2. When that directory equals the current directory, `src/nvim/path.c:2121` returns a pointer to the terminating `NUL`—effectively `\"\"`.\r\n  3. `src/nvim/fileio.c:2369` accepts that empty result and assigns it to `b_sfname`/`b_fname`.\r\n  4. `:mksession` checks only `b_fname != NULL`, then prefers the empty short name in `src/nvim/ex_session.c:252`. The result is `badd +N `.\r\n\r\n  That also explains why `try_open()` was insufficient. It works at the directory-plugin layer, while `:edit` goes through `do_ecmd()`, buffer matching/loading, `fname_expand()`, and\r\n  the normal buffer events. Additionally, `try_open()` can reject restored `buftype=nowrite` buffers. Finally, SessionLoadPost occurs after the invalid `:badd` has already executed.\r\n\r\n  The best fix is probably in `shorten_buf_fname()`:\r\n\r\n```c\r\n  char *p = path_shorten_fname(buf->b_ffname, dirname);\r\n  if (p != NULL && *p != NUL) {\r\n    buf->b_sfname = xstrdup(p);\r\n    buf->b_fname = buf->b_sfname;\r\n  } else {\r\n    buf->b_fname = buf->b_ffname;\r\n  }\r\n```\r\n  This preserves the useful invariant: a buffer with a nonempty full filename must not acquire an empty effective filename. There is precedent for this behavior:\r\n  `path_try_shorten_fname()` already rejects both `NULL` and an empty shortening result.\r\n</details>\r\n",
            "commit_id": "a929360f328fbd1e2a3fab4099a27b2a37ca5aff",
            "created_at": "2026-07-25T18:07:41Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -73,3 +73,18 @@ nvim_on('VimEnter', group, {\n     end\n   end\n end)\n+\n+nvim_on('SessionLoadPost', group, {\n+  pattern = '*',\n+  desc = 'Open directory buffers',\n+  nested = true,\n+}, function()\n+  for _, buf in ipairs(api.nvim_list_bufs()) do\n+    local name = api.nvim_buf_get_name(buf)\n+    if should_open(buf, name) then\n+      api.nvim_buf_call(buf, function()\n+        vim.cmd({ cmd = 'edit', args = { name } })",
